  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1222 PM CDT Mon Jul 13 2026\n\nThe main story today remains the persistent, dangerous heat across \nthe region. The upper ridge does not appear to weaken or budge until \nThursday at the earliest. A weak cold front is now slated for \nFriday/Friday night on the global models. Timing has been \ninconsistent with this sfc feature, though there is higher \nconfidence in some movement of the sfc high/upper ridge by Sunday. \n\nWinds will be the mitigating factor for heat indices through the \nwork week. Breezy southwest winds will usher in drier, hotter air. \nThe lower dewpoints across central SD will result in lower min RH \nthrough Wednesday. The winds will also help quickly dry out fuels as \nthe lower dewpoints spread east toward the James Valley through mid \nweek. While only Corson and Dewey counties are in the Red Flag \nWarning this afternoon, when winds increase to 25 to 35 mph gusts on \nWednesday, more counties may merit consideration for fire headlines \naround the Missouri. \n\nNo changes planned to the current headlines at this time. Blended in \nsome ConsShort to limit GFS dry/hot bias on temperatures today and \nTuesday. No change in messaging planned.",
